Quebec QSO Party - the 17 administrative regions of Quebec (the rules Appendix I)
Each region is its own multiplier for EVERY entrant, so no region maps to Qc
The rules - For all stations, one multiplier point is given for each first contact made in each administrative region
QC itself is not a valid entry (Appendix II), so nothing here answers to QC or VE2
No INCLUDE here - an out-of-province entrant loads only this file, and the host-area rule reads it
No line of this header may hold an equals sign - the reader takes any such line as an entry
https://quebecqsoparty.org/rules-quebec-qso-party/

BSA = BSA,^Bas-Saint-Laurent
SLS = SLS,^Saguenay-Lac-Saint-Jean
QUE = QUE,^Capitale-Nationale
MAU = MAU,^Mauricie
ETE = ETE,^Estrie
MTL = MTL,^Montreal
OTS = OTS,^Outaouais
ATE = ATE,^Abitibi-Temiscamingue
CND = CND,^Cote-Nord
NDQ = NDQ,^Nord-du-Quebec
GIM = GIM,^Gaspesie-Iles-de-la-Madeleine
CAS = CAS,^Chaudiere-Appalaches
LVL = LVL,^Laval
LDE = LDE,^Lanaudiere
LNS = LNS,^Laurentides
MEE = MEE,^Monteregie
CDQ = CDQ,^Centre-du-Quebec
